.TH geectl-remote-repo-add 1  "geectl-remote-repo-add 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-repo\-add \- Add a repository to a project. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the addition
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote repo\-add\fR [\fB\-\-disable\-publish\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-arch\fR> <\fB\-\-path\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a repository to a project. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the addition
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-arch\fR \fI<ARCH>\fR
An architecture the repository builds for (repeatable; at least one is required)
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
A rebuild source as `PROJECT/REPOSITORY` (repeatable; at least one is required)
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-publish\fR
Disable publishing for the added repository
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to add the repository to
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The repository name
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
